      "id": "GENUS_CATHARTES",
      "name": "Cathartes",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "A genus of three medium-sized vultures with highly developed olfactory senses, a rare adaptation among raptors that allows them to locate carrion by scent. Their naked heads and dark plumage are classic vulture traits, and they are among the most efficient scavengers in the Americas.",
